./chapters/01-connected-product-operations.html:70:<p>Year one fails the owner-income gate and should: three pilot clients cannot pay a senior founder and build the method. The mature case passes only if three delivery engineers can support twenty customers while the founder moves to sales, escalation and product. That is roughly seven customers per delivery engineer, a capacity assumption to test with time logs. If each customer consumes a day a week, the model collapses into a consultancy.</p>
./chapters/02-white-label-product-security.html:82:<p>Acquisition repeats only when enabled partners originate qualified work without founder prospecting. Delivery is teachable only when another reviewer can reproduce a finding and the partner can explain it. Value recurs because components, releases, vulnerabilities and support state change. The asset accumulates only when the next engagement becomes faster without reusing confidential customer material. If quality requires the founder on every client call, the channel has multiplied meetings, not capacity.</p>
./chapters/02-white-label-product-security.html:83:<p>The partner-removal defence must be operational. Do not withhold knowledge; that destroys trust. Instead remain useful through maintained analysis environments, cross-client pattern knowledge, surge capacity, independent review, insurer-friendly controls, and continuously updated mappings. Give the partner an exit pack and customer-data export. A partner that stays only because departure is painful will eventually leave angrily; a partner that stays because the back office is cheaper and safer than rebuilding may compound.</p>
./chapters/02-white-label-product-security.html:92:<p>The response is not to promise exclusivity across Benelux. It is to make partner success measurable: protected account, wholesale rate card, response SLA, two trained partner leads, joint quality review, and a six-month minimum once an end customer starts recurring operations. If a partner refuses training, controlled client access and responsibility boundaries while demanding a deep discount, it is shopping for invisible liability capacity, not building a channel.</p>
./chapters/02-white-label-product-security.html:115:<p>The assumption most able to reverse it is that an enabled partner will keep buying recurring specialist capacity instead of internalising the routine work and retaining the full margin.</p>
