./drafts/reviews/02-codex.err:654:<p>Acquisition repeats only when enabled partners originate qualified work without founder prospecting. Delivery is teachable only when another reviewer can reproduce a finding and the partner can explain it. Value recurs because components, releases, vulnerabilities and support state change. The asset accumulates only when the next engagement becomes faster without reusing confidential customer material. If quality requires the founder on every client call, the channel has multiplied meetings, not capacity.</p>
./drafts/reviews/02-codex.err:655:<p>The partner-removal defence must be operational. Do not withhold knowledge; that destroys trust. Instead remain useful through maintained analysis environments, cross-client pattern knowledge, surge capacity, independent review, insurer-friendly controls, and continuously updated mappings. Give the partner an exit pack and customer-data export. A partner that stays only because departure is painful will eventually leave angrily; a partner that stays because the back office is cheaper and safer than rebuilding may compound.</p>
