+
+9. **Withthegrid, “Managing grid congestion in the Netherlands with local control strategies.”**
+   URL: https://withthegrid.com/teleport/whitepaper/
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: Withthegrid's marketed local-control surface (`06-withthegrid`).
+
+10. **Scholt Energy, “Flex Services for Energy Assets.”**
+    URL: https://scholt.com/flex-services-for-energy-assets-scholt-energy
+    Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+    Supports: Scholt's marketed VPP and flexibility service surface (`06-scholt`).
+
+11. **Enervalis, customer portal.**
+    URL: https://portal.enervalis.com/
+    Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+    Supports: the portal's own marketing line only (`06-enervalis`).
+
+## Evidence boundary
+
+No source in this record establishes that a blocked business park will pay the proposed diagnostic or recurring service price; that an installer or adviser will retain a separate wholesale line; that a group will grant sufficient data and operating rights; or who bears damages for a control failure. These are the paid-test gates, not market facts. Programme budgets and contract availability are not evidence of any of them.

