+# Essay 6 — source index
+
+Accessed 2026-09-02. Vendor pages support only their described marketing surface; they are not used as evidence of customer outcomes, prices or market share.
+
+1. **Autoriteit Consument & Markt, “ACM: Energiehubs kunnen groepstransportovereenkomst aanvragen bij hun netbeheerder.”**
+   URL: https://www.acm.nl/nl/publicaties/acm-energiehubs-kunnen-groepstransportovereenkomst-aanvragen-bij-hun-netbeheerder
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: the live GTO application route and shared-capacity description (`06-gto-final`).
+
+2. **Liander, “Groepscontracten: zo werkt het.”**
+   URL: https://www.liander.nl/grootzakelijk/energietransitie/samenwerken/transportovereenkomst-voor-groepen
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: current Liander conditions, group process, GTV and stated timing (`06-liander-route`).
+
+3. **Enexis Netbeheer, “Groepstransportovereenkomst (GTO).”**
+   URL: https://www.enexis.nl/zakelijk/netcapaciteit/flexibiliteitsoplossingen/groepstransportovereenkomst
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: GTO mechanics, EMS need, present pilots and expected wider availability (`06-enexis-gto`, `06-enexis-rollout`).
+
+4. **Autoriteit Consument & Markt, “ACM stelt maatregelen tegen netcongestie vast en publiceert uitgangspunten voor toekomstige tariefaanpassingen.”**
+   URL: https://www.acm.nl/nl/publicaties/acm-stelt-maatregelen-tegen-netcongestie-vast-en-publiceert-uitgangspunten-voor-toekomstige-tariefaanpassingen
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: 1 April 2025 time-block availability and 85% duration-bound high-voltage form (`06-atr-date`).
+
+5. **Autoriteit Consument & Markt, “Voortgangsdashboard, bestuurlijke afspraken en verbeterplannen netbeheerders.”**
+   URL: https://www.acm.nl/nl/publicaties/voortgangsdashboard-bestuurlijke-afspraken-en-verbeterplannen-netbeheerders
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: current definitions of CBC, CSC, group forms, TBTR, TDTR and VVTR (`06-contract-taxonomy`).
+
+6. **Liander, “Keuzehulp deelname congestiemanagement.”**
+   URL: https://www.liander.nl/grootzakelijk/energietransitie/alles-over-netcongestie/keuzehulp-deelnemen-congestiemanagement
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: CBC forms, redispatch, GOPACS and CSP route (`06-liander-cbc`).
+
+7. **Rijksoverheid, “Maatregelen tegen vol elektriciteitsnet (netcongestie).”**
+   URL: https://www.rijksoverheid.nl/themas/klimaat-milieu-en-natuur/duurzame-energie/kabinet-neemt-maatregelen-tegen-vol-elektriciteitsnet-netcongestie
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: stated public funding envelopes, distinguished here from customer budget (`06-public-support`).
+
+8. **Sympower, “Turn your energy into profit.”**
+   URL: https://sympower.net/
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: Sympower's marketed integration, aggregation, optimisation and trading surface (`06-sympower`).
+
+9. **Withthegrid, “Managing grid congestion in the Netherlands with local control strategies.”**
+   URL: https://withthegrid.com/teleport/whitepaper/
+   Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+   Supports: Withthegrid's marketed local-control surface (`06-withthegrid`).
+
+10. **Scholt Energy, “Flex Services for Energy Assets.”**
+    URL: https://scholt.com/flex-services-for-energy-assets-scholt-energy
+    Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+    Supports: Scholt's marketed VPP and flexibility service surface (`06-scholt`).
+
+11. **Enervalis, customer portal.**
+    URL: https://portal.enervalis.com/
+    Accessed: 2026-09-02.
+    Supports: the portal's own marketing line only (`06-enervalis`).
+
+## Evidence boundary
+
+No source in this record establishes that a blocked business park will pay the proposed diagnostic or recurring service price; that an installer or adviser will retain a separate wholesale line; that a group will grant sufficient data and operating rights; or who bears damages for a control failure. These are the paid-test gates, not market facts. Programme budgets and contract availability are not evidence of any of them.
